  "ed_diag_pedido": "WHAT TO RETURN:\nThe whole corrected plan, in the SAME format (# header, @ subject :: weight, + topic :: weight :: reason). No comments, no markdown, no code fences.\n\nRULES:\n1. Subject weights (1 to 5) MUST VARY, based on the number of questions or points in the exam.\n2. Never delete a topic: if one is irrelevant, give it weight 1 and say why.\n3. Every topic needs the third field with the REASON, up to 12 words. Never invent one. If you don't know, LEAVE THE FIELD OUT — a generic phrase repeated across dozens of topics is worse than empty, because it hides how many you could actually justify.\n4. A topic merging several subjects must be split into its own lines.\n5. A topic repeated in two subjects stays only in the more appropriate one.\n\nWHERE TO PASTE THE ANSWER: in the app, Syllabus mode, button \"Paste corrected plan\". It checks that no topic was lost before replacing.",
